      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic-stability records show low hepatic extraction or scarce metabolism for related sulfonamide diuretics (bumetanide negligible hepatic extraction C72; furosemide scarcely metabolized in human hepatocytes C81; azosemide low rat microsomal CLint C75/C74 and low M1 formation CLint C76) and low intrinsic clearance/no oxidative metabolism for lorazepam/oxazepam (C73/C77/C82/C83), supporting that hepatic first-pass loss is unlikely to drive F below 20% for a related sulfonamide diuretic.",
