  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >=20%) because the closest structural analog hydrochlorothiazide shows substantial oral exposure in humans (L3), L1 gold contexts support F >=30-83% for sulfonamide-related drugs, and L6 hepatic clearance/metabolic-stability records for related sulfonamide diuretics show low hepatic extraction/scarce metabolism, reducing first-pass concern; no affirmative evidence establishes F<20% for chlorothiazide, and the unfavorable passive-permeability prior is insufficient to override this context."
}

